<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<!--
	Project-level UnrealBuildTool configuration.

	Why UBA is off here:
	  On this machine UBA (Unreal Build Accelerator) fails its file-replacement step:
	      UbaSessionServer - SetFileInformationByHandle (FileDispositionInfo) failed ... (Access is denied.)
	  The shared PCH therefore never lands on disk, and every compile after it dies with
	      fatal error C1083: cannot open precompiled header file ...: permission denied

	  Setting it here fixes every entry point at once - Build.bat, Visual Studio builds,
	  RunUAT/BuildCookRun, and Schola's `project` simulator (which invokes UBT itself and
	  offers no way to pass -NoUBA from the command line).

	  Measured on this machine: editor target builds in ~78 s clean / ~9 s incremental with
	  UBA disabled, versus a hard failure with it enabled.

	  Element names matter - UBT rejects unknown ones. `bUseUBA` is NOT valid; UBT reports
	  it as an invalid child element and lists the real names. `bAllowUBAExecutor` is the
	  one that matters here. `bAllowUBALocalExecutor` also exists but is deprecated as of
	  5.7, so it is deliberately not set.

	  If a future engine or driver update fixes the underlying access issue, flip this back
	  to true and re-measure - UBA is a genuine build-time win when it works.
-->
<Configuration xmlns="https://www.unrealengine.com/BuildConfiguration">
	<BuildConfiguration>
		<bAllowUBAExecutor>false</bAllowUBAExecutor>
	</BuildConfiguration>
</Configuration>
